---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Layerwatch"
  description="The terms that govern your use of layerwatch.dev and Layerwatch's tools."
>

  <!-- Header -->
  <div class="fixed top-4 sm:top-6 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 z-50 w-[calc(100%-2rem)] max-w-6xl">
    <header class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 sm:px-7 h-16 rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface/70 backdrop-blur-md shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)]">
      <a href="/"><img src="/logo-header.png" alt="Layerwatch" class="h-14 w-auto" /></a>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/layerwatch"
        class="hidden sm:inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-text-muted text-sm hover:text-white transition-colors"
      >
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 .5C5.73.5.75 5.48.75 11.75c0 5.02 3.26 9.28 7.77 10.78.57.1.78-.25.78-.55 0-.27-.01-1.16-.02-2.1-3.16.69-3.83-1.34-3.83-1.34-.52-1.31-1.26-1.66-1.26-1.66-1.03-.7.08-.69.08-.69 1.14.08 1.74 1.17 1.74 1.17 1.01 1.73 2.65 1.23 3.3.94.1-.73.4-1.23.72-1.51-2.52-.29-5.17-1.26-5.17-5.6 0-1.24.44-2.25 1.17-3.04-.12-.29-.51-1.45.11-3.02 0 0 .96-.31 3.14 1.16a10.9 10.9 0 0 1 5.72 0c2.18-1.47 3.14-1.16 3.14-1.16.62 1.57.23 2.73.11 3.02.73.79 1.17 1.8 1.17 3.04 0 4.35-2.66 5.31-5.19 5.59.41.35.77 1.04.77 2.1 0 1.52-.01 2.74-.01 3.11 0 .3.2.66.79.55A11.26 11.26 0 0 0 23.25 11.75C23.25 5.48 18.27.5 12 .5Z"/></svg>
        GitHub
      </a>
    </header>
  </div>

  <main class="relative px-6 pt-40 pb-28 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <span class="eyebrow mb-4">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-4 mb-3">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-text-muted/60 text-sm mb-14 font-mono">Effective August 21, 2026</p>

    <div class="legal-content space-y-10 text-text-muted leading-relaxed">

      <section>
        <h2>Acceptance of terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing layerwatch.dev, joining the waitlist, or using any tool we publish (the browser
          extension, the MCP proxy, or any future Layerwatch product), you agree to these Terms. If you don't
          agree, please don't use our services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Description of service</h2>
        <p>
          Layerwatch provides runtime visibility and trust tooling for AI coding agents. Today that includes
          this website, an early-access waitlist, and a free, open-source browser extension. Additional tools,
          including an open-source MCP proxy, are under active development.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Early access &amp; beta disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          Our products are under active, early-stage development. Features may change, break, or be removed
          without notice, and we make no guarantee of uptime, accuracy, or continuity of service. Use in
          production environments is at your own risk.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Eligibility</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of legal majority in your jurisdiction, to use our
          services. If you're using them on behalf of an organization, you confirm you have the authority to
          bind that organization to these Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use our services for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable regulation.</li>
          <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload, or gain unauthorized access to our infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Reverse engineer our tools with the intent to bypass their security or licensing controls.</li>
          <li>Misrepresent your identity to abuse the waitlist or early-access process.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The Layerwatch name, logo, and branding are the property of Layerwatch. Source code we publish as
          open source is made available under the license included in each respective repository; where no
          license file is present, no rights beyond viewing the source are granted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party services &amp; links</h2>
        <p>
          Our site and tools may link to or rely on third-party services (for example, Formspree and
          Cloudflare). We aren't responsible for the content, policies, or practices of any third party.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
        <p>
          Our services are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, express or
          implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Layerwatch will not be liable for any indirect, incidental,
          special, or consequential damages arising from your use of, or inability to use, our services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Termination</h2>
        <p>
          We may suspend or discontinue access to any part of our services, including the waitlist, at any
          time, for any reason, without liability.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. We'll update the effective date above and, for material
          changes, notify the waitlist by email. Continued use after a change constitutes acceptance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of India, without regard to its conflict of law principles.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms? Email <a href="mailto:hi@layerwatch.dev">hi@layerwatch.dev</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="relative border-t border-border-subtle px-6 pt-16 pb-8 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-full max-w-3xl h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-primary/40 to-transparent"></div>

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto relative z-10">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-6 pb-12">
        <a href="/"><img src="/logo-header.png" alt="Layerwatch" class="h-10 w-auto self-start" /></a>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
          <p class="text-text-muted/50 text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-mono">Connect</p>
          <ul class="flex items-center gap-6 text-sm">
            <li><a href="https://github.com/layerwatch" class="text-text-muted hover:text-white transition-colors">GitHub</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://x.com/layerwatch" class="text-text-muted hover:text-white transition-colors">X</a></li>
            <li><a href="mailto:hi@layerwatch.dev" class="text-text-muted hover:text-white transition-colors">Contact</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-border-subtle flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between gap-2">
        <p class="text-text-muted/60 text-xs">© 2026 Layerwatch. All rights reserved.</p>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-text-muted/60 hover:text-white text-xs transition-colors">Privacy</a>
          <a href="/terms" class="text-text-muted/60 hover:text-white text-xs transition-colors">Terms</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-content h2 {
    color: white;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .legal-content p { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .legal-content ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-content a {
    color: var(--color-primary-light);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .legal-content a:hover { color: white; }
</style>
